    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d725">

                <pb facs="0837" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/9895a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-01T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Raleigh</hi> due to arrive at Monrovia on or about
                    May 6. Commanding officer has appropriate instructions. Report fully by cable
                    result of conference between commanding officer and Liberian authorities.
                    Department has advised British and French Governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
